        "created_at": "2025-01-01T15:15:10Z",
        "updated_at": "2025-01-01T15:15:10Z",
        "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
        "body": "I'm fine with \"manifest field\" (though I'll keep using \"definitional extension\"). I guess it's shortening that to \"field\" that bugs me!\r\n\r\nYes, I too would like some kind of 'default' mechanism. Though I think that, in Agda, one ought to be forced to prove that the alternate definition is equivalent to the default one. Which I guess means that providing a default on something with no notion of equivalence would be disallowed. It certainly would be interesting to play around with that!",
